{"title":"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Analytic_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Analytic Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Geometric_Probability)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Geometric Probability)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Triangle_Inequality)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Triangle Inequality)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An object moves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm in a straight <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">line</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, turns at an angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, measured in radians and chosen at random from the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/58120b09b09030f8626fa6fe4ccdccdd3c11654d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,\\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />, and moves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm in a straight line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. What is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Probability\" title=\"Probability\">probability</a> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7a14222d202835cdf73fe7d773f8693c6db03b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c41561fd38237faf56451aa9da24f8326b7125.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"361\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Trigonometry)\">Solution 1 (Trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa27e367ee30b29f2d1a532e31a1a179a1fce2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} AB^2 + BC^2 - 2 AB \\cdot BC \\cos \\alpha = 89 - 80 \\cos \\alpha = AC^2 &amp;&lt; 49\\\\ \\cos \\alpha &amp;&gt; \\frac 12\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"464\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d75d5bdbe1b9e3f23c326fe1f6a4bff298c8411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\alpha &lt; \\frac {\\pi}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"83\" height=\"33\" />, and the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc2c7d0343881a3c9a5058b17eaab6d851cb718e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi/3}{\\pi} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac13 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"119\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Analytic_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Analytic_Geometry)\">Solution 2 (Analytic Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Analytic Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2003AMC12BP21.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c2/2003AMC12BP21.png/500px-2003AMC12BP21.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"494\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c2/2003AMC12BP21.png/750px-2003AMC12BP21.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c2/2003AMC12BP21.png/1000px-2003AMC12BP21.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce26ae0583d170422defc83069591b472895c151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WLOG$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />, let the object turn clockwise.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943df464f6bacb9e19cddd41029163b289104bb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a06ae81e4e18d2f9c8a5dce569c7ea095e1210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (0, -8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Note that the possible points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> create a semi-circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The area where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7a14222d202835cdf73fe7d773f8693c6db03b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> is enclosed by a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7a14222d202835cdf73fe7d773f8693c6db03b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/912b7164bed3bb70d9eb449917bf52594ab21dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\angle ABO}{180 ^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>The function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/3223c53877fe552201a4329ed5f81ef58ca9eaca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d72848c7869b54f9d0f1e26cf1a8aea5e24d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />, the function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be2b97c5ae709686d6386ca0745424204cca47c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/25005407a910941243d530eefce851c53df65f17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (y+8)^2 = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the point that satisfies the system of equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/3249cd27206153e6e7c152162916d3b28157fd62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{cases} x^2 + y^2 = 25 \\\\ x^2 + (y+8)^2 = 49 \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"180\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a34d5d021ee0d81ea73f7da8d73e82a628753035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (y+8)^2 - x^2 - y^2 = 49 - 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/89849fd6097c2dbf64e8b1eb19364b44caa43417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 + 16y =24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab12758cb2a2492352b16670d8fb8e95eef61e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = - \\frac52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d81c6819409071352f7c84dc5504e8740ade38dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c37d12478cc865769a191473caee2b352f673d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O = (\\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{2}, - \\frac52)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be7a10811b43f4f2a9b80e7c6f0ed5437dc6ce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDO$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangle, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94b89b5efa49cb375e0c0071d7717badf6b1dc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BO = 5$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe5c245f34f5231855bd516fc7686c3256f2dec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afad411c0c6d092d1b04bdd5458801bed4dfbbaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DO = \\frac52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />. As a result <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/a/dea03292efe9eac6b8a9de368475fc2891d3ea6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBO = 30 ^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4ec57391ec91a48f2ff75d46129c25df234748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABO = 60 ^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7a14222d202835cdf73fe7d773f8693c6db03b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c894060766f906c7d92e99524e94241c805b9958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\angle ABO}{180 ^\\circ} = \\frac{60 ^\\circ}{180 ^\\circ} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac13 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"209\" height=\"49\" /> \n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Geometric_Probability.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Geometric_Probability)\">Solution 3 (Geometric Probability)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Geometric Probability)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b3d9b8d04d50e4d2615681c9fc75b55592a7e43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cbf585f69f59d04f3493bbe4bee458949fa00e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (8,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />, after assuming segment AB to be straight in the x-direction relative to our coordinate system (in other words, due to symmetrically we can set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/4/62434ae80ca145c20f0fbc7563f5151371ed163c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> for point B). This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/2/a425ebb28b89be23346ec55e1937f55976844ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (8 + 5cos(\\alpha), 5sin(\\alpha))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />. Using the distance formula we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f645f835a5e242ffdab9f4af243d1c5edf7a8db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sqrt((8 + 5cos(\\alpha))^2 + (5sin(\\alpha))^2) &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"299\" height=\"21\" />. After algebra, this simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/f/fdff032d345b30fe1ab413c8a5324f068605bd8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cos(\\alpha) &lt; -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" />. After evaluating the constraints of the problem, we land on option (D).\n</p><p>~PeterDoesPhysics\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Triangle_Inequality.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Triangle_Inequality)\">Solution 4 (Triangle Inequality)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Triangle Inequality)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that we can treat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99f70910687ba4a3b24f368749244137a14c5b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> as a triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b5000627d977251fab80100e224f275486eb94c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=x.$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> are not part of the interval of valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> values, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e93ef027bb0409be09d6e1da48f228e943d540bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle \\text{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> is a non-degenerate triangle. Then, by the Triangle Inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b7f995a366904d1ff2cc2ac50edfb39050b0d62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+8&gt;x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/0664fdab42a5b90b1ba0ec467009fe71a6bc37a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+x&gt;8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a05acf51cb37a178b83bdd7bba2b82b8eb26e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+x&gt;5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> These reduce to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/884ae83400e1fa5efe36aea21c186af1348af624.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e1f23f96ece65cb1a5ce4e1df2d90f974a88ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25b57d927be7f45439934660a9c3dc4c68b5283.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;-3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" /> Thus, the possible values of x are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df17e938645eeb948bc405d67baea89f1c241563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3&lt;x&lt;13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3d812502315ba86a623971e80f13c5ddafe7b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\text{[}4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12\\text{]}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" /> Of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/43420adcd0fce9dce3978d53b97a8e0262b58da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> so the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7deb79cdfc8a507ba781678bfef89b608bb8f4c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8438128eaebee10ffcc6e41a8be6e5e72c2394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac39=\\frac13=\\boxed{\\text{(D)}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~~AndrewZhong2012~~\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B\">2003 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a